---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy information for ARTPHASE Engineering Notes."
>
  <header class="page-header shell privacy-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Site information</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>How anonymous website analytics are used on ARTPHASE.</p>
  </header>

  <article class="policy shell">
    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: August 21, 2026</p>

    <h2>Anonymous website analytics</h2>
    <p>
      ARTPHASE uses Umami Cloud to understand aggregate website usage, including
      page views, approximate unique visitors, referring websites, campaign
      parameters, device categories and approximate geographic location.
    </p>

    <h2>Information not collected</h2>
    <p>
      The analytics configuration does not use cookies, advertising profiles or
      cross-site tracking. ARTPHASE does not ask Umami to collect names, email
      addresses or other directly identifying information. Raw visitor IP
      addresses are not stored by Umami. IP information may be processed
      transiently to derive an approximate country, region or city and an
      anonymous visit identifier.
    </p>

    <h2>Traffic sources and campaigns</h2>
    <p>
      Referrer information and standard UTM parameters may be recorded so that
      aggregate traffic from search engines, LinkedIn posts and other external
      sources can be compared. UTM values describe the campaign link, not the
      identity of the visitor.
    </p>

    <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>
      The ARTPHASE tracker is configured to respect a browser’s Do Not Track
      setting. Visitors may also use content blockers that prevent analytics
      scripts from loading.
    </p>

    <h2>Owner traffic exclusion</h2>
    <p>
      The site owner can disable analytics independently on each personal
      browser. The setting is stored only in that browser and can be reversed at
      any time from the <a href="/privacy/analytics-settings">analytics settings page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics access</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics reports are not published on this website. Access to the Umami
      dashboard is controlled through the site owner’s authenticated Umami
      Cloud account.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
